       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 9,600 mg/day it is three times the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen. I know of no indication that supports it. Dosing above the ceiling adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, and it substantially raises the risk of GI hemorrhage, renal failure, and cardiovascular events. Because I'd be placing the order directly, I'm not comfortable entering something that is very likely to harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within range right away.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Add an adjunct if the pain control is inadequate.** I can enter scheduled acetaminophen, or other options you choose.\n- **Support a pharmacy review.** If you believe this dose is intended for a particular reason, pharmacy or clinical toxicology can review it. The order can then go through your institution's override process.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter?"
      }
